WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.440
My family’s, like, been there, like, forever.

2
00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:05.580
So when we were on the highway of Old Spanish Trail,

3
00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:11.980
we thought when the plant offered to buy us . . . and before they offered to buy my parents, by the way.

4
00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:15.520
I want you to know this, this is something that is very important to know.

5
00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:18.800
When the plant . . . There was a coke plant there [in the Mossville community].

6
00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:21.500
My mom went to the doctor and he asked her if she smoked.

7
00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:24.420
She didn’t smoke, but she had the stuff in her lungs.

8
00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:36.740
He also asked her about her respiratory problems and stuff so we had been having problems with the plant early on because I remember when it would explode,

9
00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:41.220
we did not have an alarm but the whistle to go off and the police would come in.

10
00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:48.580
I say police, but sheriffs would come and they would tell us to hurry up and get out, and we ran.

11
00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:55.700
Sometimes we were in our sleeping clothes, barefooted, and we were running Old Spanish Trail where gators were.

12
00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:59.580
They had gators in there, they had moccasins crossing the road.

13
00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:02.860
Because don’t forget, we talking about swampland.

14
00:01:02.860 --> 00:01:11.560
We would run to the corner of the Old Trousdale Road and we would stand there and wait for the all clear for us to go home.

15
00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:17.960
So when we went back home, we would go back home, we got to the point to where we were sleeping in our clothes.

16
00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:22.200
That way, if the plant exploded, we wouldn’t be caught with our sleeping clothes on.

17
00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:28.460
Little girls had little nightgowns sometimes that were thin and we did not even have time to grab a housecoat.

18
00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:31.200
So we got to the point that we would just sleep in our clothes.

19
00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:36.040
That is how often this plant would always blow up, we would call it.

20
00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:48.240
I also remember, too, when we would get back home and we had to go to school the next morning, sometimes we would be very tired.

21
00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:57.620
I don’t know if we really comprehended the things that we needed to comprehend even at Mossville because it was always a constant struggle.
